  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nThe dry southwest flow remains over the panhandles on Wednesday\nkeeping the panhandles weather calm. This will change come\nThursday as a weather system deepens across the western portions\nof CONUS. This will change the flow enough to allow a moisture\nfetch to move back across the southern plains. A passing small\nweather system within the upper level flow in addition to jet\nenergy will most likely provide lift across the panhandles late \nThursday through Saturday. This in turn will allow the formation \nof rain showers and thunderstorms during this time. This system \nthen moves off to the east on Sunday which would more likely than \nnot will taper down the chances for rain showers and \nthunderstorms.",
